The SDK sizes every receive timeout for the FTDI default 16 ms latency timer,
so a lost status packet stalls the caller for 34 ms. The plugin runs the
adapter at 1 ms, so size the timeout for it.

--- a/src/dynamixel_sdk/port_handler_linux.cpp	2026-01-15 09:45:23.000000000 +1000
+++ b/src/dynamixel_sdk/port_handler_linux.cpp	2026-09-18 18:49:27.099854716 +1000
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@
 
 #include "port_handler_linux.h"
 
-#define LATENCY_TIMER  16  // msec (USB latency timer)
+#define LATENCY_TIMER  1  // msec (USB latency timer, set to 1 ms by the payloads plugin)
                            // You should adjust the latency timer value. From the version Ubuntu 16.04.2, the default latency timer of the usb serial is '16 msec'.
                            // When you are going to use sync / bulk read, the latency timer should be loosen.
                            // the lower latency timer value, the faster communication speed.
